    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d359">

                <pb facs="0558" n="272" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg272"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/8721</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hamburg</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamburg</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-07T12:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 7, 1916, 12 noon</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 9, 1.50 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3971. Department’s telegraphic instruction May 31. German Government does not
                    intend to voluntarily institute prize court proceedings in case of S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Arabic</hi>. This equally applies to all vessels
                    destroyed by Germany in the so-called war zone. Claimants may institute
                    proceedings before prize court although monition is not issued.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
